# L §6.4: a scenario's expression row "reads inputs, bands and defs, never a place or a movement (a balance, flows, a
# move's instance), directly or through a def (LOAD-SCENARIO)". s1's row reads the base def held, which reads
# bal(konto, ...): through a def, refused. s2's row reads bal(household.konto, ...) directly: refused. s3's row reads
# the band fee: allowed (fee's one row gives 10 PLN). The base runs. (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §6.4, a prefixed place,
# band or move in an expression row.)
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2040-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
input cap: num PLN
input day0: date
band fee(x: num PLN): num PLN

def held: num PLN
  rule r = bal(konto, day0)

version base_2026
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cap = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  day0 = 2026-06-30 "own"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  fee: [0 PLN, inf) = 10.00 PLN "own"

ask c: cap law 2031-06-30
=== s1.tally
scenario s1 over household
  tally 2
  from 2031-01-01

version v1
  cite plan
  governs 2031-01-01..
  known 2026-10-20
  replace cap = household.held "z def"

ask a: cap in s1 law 2031-06-30
=== s2.tally
scenario s2 over household
  tally 2
  from 2031-01-01

version v2
  cite plan
  governs 2031-01-01..
  known 2026-10-20
  replace cap = bal(household.konto, household.day0) "z salda"

ask a: cap in s2 law 2031-06-30
=== s3.tally
scenario s3 over household
  tally 2
  from 2031-01-01

version v3
  cite plan
  governs 2031-01-01..
  known 2026-10-20
  replace cap = fee(household.cap) "z pasma"

ask a: cap in s3 law 2031-06-30
=== expect
scenario s1: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO the expression row of cap in s1 reads the place konto through held ...
scenario s2: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO household.konto: an expression row reads inputs, bands and defs, never a place ...
a: 10 PLN
  world: s3
...
c: 1 000 PLN
...
